# Pull Request Template and Linear Ticket (Mandatory)

When the agent creates a GitHub Pull Request, ALL of the following are required.

## 1. Read and fill the repo template

Before `gh pr create`, read `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md` and fill every section with real content. Do not invent a different outline (no `## Summary` / `## Test plan` substitutes).

`gh pr create` does **not** auto-apply that file. Always pass the filled markdown as the PR **description** via `--body` (HEREDOC). Never leave the body empty.

## 2. Description, never only a PR comment

- Put the filled template in the PR **description** (`--body`).
- Do **not** create the PR with an empty/short body and then post the write-up as a GitHub PR comment.

```bash
gh pr create --base develop --title "<title>" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
<filled contents of .github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md>
EOF
)"
```

Never use `--base main`. See `.cursor/rules/pull-request-base-branch.mdc`.

## 3. Linear ticket state: In Review

After the PR exists, move the matching Linear ticket (`MOC-N`) to **In Review** via Linear MCP `save_issue` (`id: "MOC-N"`, `state: "In Review"`). The Mocal App Team has no "PR created" state; **In Review** is its equivalent. Skip if it is already In Review. Never set Done, Canceled, Duplicate, or Backlog as a side effect of opening a PR.

## 4. Linear ticket comment (same template) — every PR

After the PR exists and the URL is known, post a **Linear comment** on the ticket with Linear MCP `save_comment` (`issueId: "MOC-N"`, markdown `body`). The ticket id comes from the branch `feat/MOC-n-...` or the conversation.

The comment MUST include:

1. The GitHub PR URL
2. The same filled template used as the PR description

Do this for **every** PR, including follow-up and fix PRs for the same ticket. Do not skip the comment, and do not treat the comment as a substitute for the state change (or the reverse).

## Order

1. `gh pr create` (base `develop`, filled template as `--body`)
2. `save_issue` → `In Review` (skip if already)
3. `save_comment` with PR URL + the same filled template
4. If `save_issue` or `save_comment` fails, retry once; if it still fails, tell the user (the PR already exists).

```text
✅ gh pr create --body "<filled template>" → save_issue "In Review" → save_comment (PR URL + template)
❌ Empty/short --body, then gh pr comment with the write-up
❌ Custom ## Summary / ## Test plan instead of the repo template
❌ GitHub PR without a Linear comment on MOC-N
❌ GitHub PR while Linear stays In Progress / Todo
```

Write the PR description and the Linear comment in English (see `.cursor/rules/documentation-english.mdc`).
